WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.360
Whether it's an X-Men film, the next chapter
in the MCU, or an entry in the DC Extended

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:09.040
Universe, superhero movies are filled with
some truly incredible moments.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.400
These films are about super-poweredbeings
who fight crime, serve justice, and provide

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:14.840
humanity with hope.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:19.160
As a result, they've given us all kinds of
epic moments and stunning visuals that'll

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.340
make you want to slam that pause button.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.000
It all started in 2008, when Tony Stark announced:

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.320
"I am Iron Man."

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:34.320
After that, we were introduced to a green
rage monster, a star-spangled soldier, the

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.700
god of thunder, and two deadly assassins.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.640
But we hadn't seen them all together yet,
until The Avengers came along.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.600
Directed by Joss Whedon, this 2012 mega-hit
assembled Earth's mightiest heroes for the

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.480
very first time.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:50.700
They bickered, they bantered, they battled
aliens, and every scene built towards possibly

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.260
the greatest hero shot in cinematic history.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.260
In the final act of the film, Loki and his
Chitauri army are attacking New York City.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:01.899
Five of the six Avengers are doing their best
to hold back the aliens, but then there's

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.320
a toothy space whale joins the fray.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.820
Fortunately, that's when a bedraggled Bruce
Banner shows up.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.180
He gets mad, Hulk smashes the Leviathan, and
the angry Chitauri surround the Avengers,

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.100
letting loose with a terrifying war cry.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:16.980
But these heroes aren't afraid.

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:22.000
Instead, they all stand back-to-back, preparing
for war, as the camera circles around them

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.900
and you'll need to press pause so you can
fully revel in such an awesome moment.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:31.020
Black Panther introduced the world to Killmonger,
possibly the greatest villain to wreak havoc

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.020
in the MCU.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.899
Played by Michael B. Jordan, he's a black
ops soldier who wants the Wakandan throne,

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:39.600
but before he can rule, he must defeat King
T'Challa.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:44.280
Even though it's an incredibly advanced nation,
Wakanda still practices ritual combat.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.290
If you beat the king, you get the crown, and
Killmonger has been training his entire life

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:48.820
for this.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:52.600
As his name implies, he's been racking up
an impressive body count, and every time he

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.079
takes a life, he marks his body with a scar.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:59.380
At first, we only see a few bumps on his forearm,
but when it comes time to fight T'Challa,

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:03.320
he pops that shirt off and reveals he's absolutely
covered in little dots.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:08.050
According to Jordan, there were over 2000
of those bumps, which adds up to a lot of

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:08.580
corpses.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:13.380
It's a terrific and terrifying reveal, showing
that Killmonger is going to be the toughest

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.380
challenge that T'Challa has ever faced.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:19.400
On top of that, seeing Killmonger in all his
glory prompted quite a bit of thirst from

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.400
Michael B. Jordan fans.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:23.720
"Every time I think about Michael B. Jordan
my uterus bursts into flames."

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:24.280
"Oh, man!"

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.970
The airport battle in Captain America: Civil
War might be the greatest comic book movie

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.040
moment of all time.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.760
All these heroes are coming together for an
epic showdown.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.460
Nobody wants to kill anyone, and they're mostly
friends, so they're going to exchange as many

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.460
quips as kicks.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:43.300
Still, that doesn't stop them from shooting
arrows, tossing cars, and blowing things up.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.300
As a result, you've got a fun-filled action
scene filled with pause-worthy moments that

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.190
need some extra appreciation.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:53.800
For example, there's the first appearance
of the MCU's new Spider-Man, the moment that

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:57.960
Giant-Man snags War Machine out of the air,
and any time that Black Panther is going to

00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:58.460
town.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:03.460
But the scene that deserves the most attention
comes when both groups finally square off.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.160
When it becomes clear that Cap's team isn't
backing down, the two groups rush at each

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.540
other for a superhero extravaganza.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.980
As the Avengers battle each other in this
melee of epic proportions, the pause button

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:17.480
will come in handy if you want to see who
fights whom, how they're using their powers,

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.920
and who's the toughest hero in this crazy
civil war.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.360
When you're playing the Joker, you've got
to make a big entrance.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:28.140
And on that score, it's hard to compete with
Heath Ledger's strange and scary intro in

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.140
The Dark Knight.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:34.320
In one of the best opening scenes of all time,
a gang of robbers, all wearing clown masks,

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.940
hit one of the biggest banks in Gotham.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:39.600
But as they deactivate the alarm system and
crack the safe, we hear them talking about

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:42.420
their murderous and mysterious employer: the
Joker.

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:46.710
The clown thieves whisper about how the Joker
wears warpaint and how he's totally crazy.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:51.180
He's also quite dangerous, as he's ordered
the robbers to pick each other off, one by

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:51.680
one.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.140
Eventually, there's only one clown left, and
he's about to make his big getaway, when he

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.820
hears somebody screaming after him.

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:01.780
It's the bank manager, and he's none too impressed
with these mask-wearing thugs.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.550
And that's when we get the money shot.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:07.600
The clown gets in the bank manager's face
and pulls off his mask to reveal that, yes

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:09.620
indeed, he is the Joker.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.640
He's got greasy hair, darkened eyes, and big
scars.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.040
It's then that you'll want to pause the film
so you can admire that impeccably choreographed

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:21.060
heist, and also so that you can calm down
after staring straight into the eyes of chaos.

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:26.260
Tony Stark has always been the most complicated
Avenger, but when he first appeared in 2008's

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.200
Iron Man, he was a straight-up jerk.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.960
He was completely self-centered and amoral,
and he made his living as a "merchant of death."

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:37.390
He sold weapons of mass destruction, and until
he was captured by terrorists, he didn't care

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.900
where his missiles ended up.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:42.820
Despite all this, his obnoxious attitude gave
us one of the most pause-worthy moments in

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.300
the MCU: when he proudly presents his Jericho
missiles.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:51.400
Ever the showman, Tony gives a razzle-dazzle
speech to a group of Army officers as he fires

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.570
his weapon into an Afghani desert.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.880
The missile opens mid-air and sends a dozen
tiny rockets tumbling down into the mountains

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:58.380
below.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:03.920
As they ignite some massive explosions, Tony
spreads his arms like a circus ringmaster,

00:05:03.930 --> 00:05:06.420
and it's here that you'll want to press pause.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.590
The smoke is billowing in the background,
the shock wave is heading straight for the

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:12.140
camera, and Tony's hubris is on full display.

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:16.920
Director Christopher Nolan has a knack for
creating truly staggering visuals.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:21.440
And one of the most breathtaking is the burning
Bat Symbol in The Dark Knight Rises.

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:24.590
This 2012 flick finds Gotham City in a world
of trouble.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.990
The villainous Bane has taken over, and he's
holding everybody hostage with a neutron bomb.

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:33.880
He's cut off all escape routes, trapped the
police in the sewer system, and worse still,

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.180
he recently broke Batman's back and tossed
him into an underground prison.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:41.340
Things are looking grim for the citizens of
Gotham, especially Commissioner Gordon, who's

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:45.230
about to get iced, and that's when Batman
shows up to save the day.

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:49.430
You can't keep a good bat down, and after
Batman fixes his back and escapes the pit,

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:51.820
he rescues Gordon from his incredibly cold
fate.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.800
But the rest of the city needs to know help
is on the way, so the two crimefighters light

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:59.490
a giant flaming Bat Symbol atop a nearby bridge.

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:03.020
The burning logo gives everyone hope, and
it's such a powerful shot that it's worth

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.120
pausing the film to admire the flames.

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.900
Hugh Jackman joined the X-Men in 2000, and
he proceeded to play the cigar-chomping Wolverine

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:11.540
for over 16 years.

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:16.670
In fact, he holds the Guinness world record
for "longest career as a live-action Marvel

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.660
superhero," along with his X-Men co-star Patrick
Stewart.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:24.940
So when it came time for Jackman to say goodbye
in Logan, it broke a lot of Marvel fans' hearts.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:28.139
Fortunately, the 2017 film gave the character
a proper goodbye.

00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:31.770
He went out fighting, protecting children
from an evil band of scientists and soldiers,

00:06:31.770 --> 00:06:35.270
and he was sent off with one of cinema's most
emotional eulogies.

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:39.150
With tears welling in her eyes, the young
Laura stands over Logan's grave and delivers

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.840
a monologue from the classic western film
Shane.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.220
"Tell her everything's all right.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:49.500
There are no more guns in the valley."

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:54.900
After the speech, she reaches over to Logan's
grave marker and flips it on its side, turning

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.460
a cross into an "X."

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.020
You'll want to hit the pause button here because
the tears will be flowing, and you'll also

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:04.830
want to marvel at that final shot of the grave,
a tender farewell to the most famous of the

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:05.320
X-Men.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.400
Ever since the credits of the first Avengers
film, Marvel fans knew Thanos was coming.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:15.180
The Mad Titan finally made his move in Avengers:
Infinity War, rounding up all the Infinity

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:18.660
Stones and halving the population of the universe
with a single snap.

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.800
But before that heartbreaking moment, the
Avengers did their best to stop the purple

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.050
warlord, and none were quite as effective
as Dr. Strange.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:30.230
The surgeon-turned-sorcerer was a key player
in Infinity War, protecting the Time Stone

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:33.200
from the Black Order and battling Thanos himself
on Titan.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.040
And it's on this desolate planet that Strange's
powers are on full display.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:41.340
He opens portals for Spider-Man to jump through,
he helps Star-Lord run through the air, and

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.900
his cloak even gets in on the action.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:47.690
In fact, the best moment of the Titan fight
is when Strange and Thanos go mano-a-mano.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:52.530
The most pause-worthy image comes when Strange
sprouts multiple arms to perform the Images

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.200
of Ikonn.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.520
You'll want to hit pause again when there
are about 100 Dr. Strange's attacking Thanos

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.280
with 100 Eldritch Whips.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:03.020
Basically, any time Strange and Thanos are
throwing down, you'll want to pause the movie

00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:04.360
and admire the magic.

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:10.820
As played by Gal Gadot, Wonder Woman, a.k.a.
Diana Prince, was both kind and courageous,

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:11.900
gentle and deadly.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.919
She was a compassionate god-killer, and we
got to see both sides on display during one

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:20.260
of the greatest action scenes in superhero
history: the battle of No Man's Land.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:24.940
During a mission to stop an evil German general,
Diana learns that a village full of innocents

00:08:24.949 --> 00:08:26.750
has been captured by enemy troops.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.880
Putting her mission on hold, she decides to
rescue the helpless villagers by walking across

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.070
the most dangerous stretch of ground on the
Western Front.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.940
With the help of her bulletproof bracelets,
she storms across No Man's Land, blocking

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:41.120
shots and deflecting bombs like it's an afternoon
stroll through the park.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:45.140
As Diana walks through explosions and streaks
of flame, you'll need to press the pause button

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.640
multiple times to fully absorb her awesomeness.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.740
There's the scene when she steps onto the
battlefield in her full Wonder Woman regalia.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:55.260
There's the moment when she blocks the first
bullet, and then there's the scene when she

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:59.020
pulls out that shield and stops a barrage
of machine gun blasts.

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:03.350
It's maybe the most inspirational scene in
any DC movie, and any time you press pause,

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.540
you can't help but stare in wonder.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:11.140
In the 2018 animated film Spider-Man: Into
the Spider-Verse, there's no scene more visually

00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:14.700
impressive than the moment Miles Morales finally
takes a leap of faith.

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:18.600
Throughout the film, this teenager has been
struggling with way more than any kid should

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:19.440
ever have to deal with.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:23.260
He's suddenly gotten super powers, but he
doesn't know how to use them, and he's scared

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:24.940
he might never live up to his potential.

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:28.780
On top of all that, there are supervillains
trying to kill him, which never makes things

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:29.280
easier.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:33.760
Grappling with his dual identities, Miles
finally owns his Spider-persona, adapting

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:38.700
his suit to fit his own background and personality,
before literally taking a leap off an enormous

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:39.700
skyscraper.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:44.430
As Miles free-falls through the air, he passes
through a gorgeous cityscape lit with neon

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:46.860
blues, dark purples, and smooth pinks.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.920
He's directly at the center of the frame,
surrounded by giant, hulking buildings.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:55.280
The world seems so big, Miles seems so small,
and he's falling so fast.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:10:00.480
But when he blasts those web shooters and
begins swinging through the city, he is Spider-Man.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:04.110
He's done more than enough to earn the cover
to his own comic, and this scene has done

00:10:04.110 --> 00:10:06.700
more than enough to earn a few admiring pauses.

